{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"344393de8d9a2378b3ecf99207c398d879228e61d18da8ff5731e34991239942","digest":{"component_or_area":"Cloud adapter fetcher enrichment boundary","key_entities":["RunawayPaginationError","BackendPaginationStallError","adapters/jira/acli_graph.py","fetcher.py:625","fetcher.py:672","fetcher.py:712","fetch_snapshot","get_parent_map","get_comment_map","get_issuelinks_map","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_graph_pagination_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["pagination stall","error swallowing","exception hierarchy","fail-open handler","snapshot degradation","type mismatch"],"propositions":["RunawayPaginationError subclasses RuntimeError instead of BackendPaginationStallError, placing it outside the core stall hierarchy","fetch_snapshot's three enrichment re-raise clauses match only on BackendPaginationStallError, causing Cloud stalls to miss all three re-raise handlers and fall through to broad except Exception fail-opens","When a Cloud cursor stalls during parent/comment/issuelink enrichment, the error is logged as a warning and a silently degraded snapshot is written instead of propagating the stall","Making RunawayPaginationError subclass BackendPaginationStallError allows the three fetcher re-raise clauses to catch and propagate Cloud stalls while preserving existing except RuntimeError sites"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787718544081537001,"uuid":"213b2c78-844c-4167-ae76-aedb229562f5"}